review_comments.body:
Here's the test I tried within an `ajaxTest()` call, which always fails (s.contentType is "application/json"):

```
return {
	url: "bogus.html",
	contentType: "application/json",
	headers: { "content-type": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded" },
	beforeSend: function( _, s ) {
		assert.strictEqual( s.contentType, "application/x-www-form-urlencoded", "contentType is overwritten" );
		return false;
	},
	error: true
};
```
Is there something obvious I'm doing wrong?

The %20 tests indirectly check whether the prefilter works, so at least we have coverage of that code (?).

