When making the changes after the rebase, I noticed tests are finishing a bit too quickly. Then I realized I forgot to update the `dir` definition. I added some validation that anything got run.

It'd be a bit safer to also print a list of files with tests that are executed as then if wrong ones were run, I'd notice immediately. This would make the output here a bit longer, though, and we don't have a good mechanism for verbose mode so I didn't add anything like that.

@timmywil what do you think? Should we print the list of test files?

