review_comments.body:
This method is risky IMO. The defaults will only apply to destructured variables like `modules` or `retries` but the `options` object contains them as they were passed. I suspect this may be a problem since you pass `options` to a few APIs as-is.

It'd be safer to keep destructuring directly in parameters. If you then need the `options` object to be fully passed in some places, you can always define it here instead of destructuring:
```js
	const options = {
		amd,
		browsers: browserNames,
		/* ... */
	};
```
The main drawback is each parameter appears twice but the risk above disappears.

